	(text "Power / hold slider, OFF - HOLD - ON:\nOFF pulls 3V3_EN low: TPS63802 off (so the MCU,\nand with it VS_EN: VS1053 LDOs off too). DRV2605L off\ntoo. Charger and gauge stay on the battery.\nHOLD pulls LOCK_SW (PE3) low. Going from ON to OFF\npasses HOLD: save state, finish SD writes there."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 133.35 49.53 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "049dc081-a5c2-43ba-a551-fc5438e1ca77")
	)
	(text "Haptics: DRV2605L, 10 mm coin ERM on M+/M- pads.\n+3.3V -> JP502 (cut to measure) -> DRV_VDD. I2C1 at 0x5A.\nEN = DRV_EN (PB5), R509 pull-down: shutdown while the\nMCU is off. IN/TRIG to GND (internal trigger)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 133.35 156.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "128696ff-b426-4287-b616-30f433c3b748")
	)
	(text "MPR121"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.75 192.532 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2aa34891-87e2-4e4e-b035-96fa45e01634")
	)
	(text "Click wheel buttons"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 139.192 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4ea78804-54aa-4da4-b5a3-1ff9f8026d4c")
	)
	(text "Electrodes connections"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 39.116 62.992 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "506e932d-8f2d-46f0-a6f1-befd42811a30")
	)
	(text "Same core as the Adafruit MPR121 breakout (github.com/adafruit/Adafruit-MPR121-PCB):\nVREG 100n, REXT 75k, ~IRQ 10k pull-up. No regulator / level shifter: 3.3V only.\nADDR on VDD: 0x5B. I2C1 pull-ups are on the MCU sheet.\nElectrodes: ELE0 right, ELE1 left, ELE2 top, ELE3 bottom (software/src/ClickWheel.hpp),\nELE4 center (spare for now). ELE5-11 free (GPIO/LED drivers if needed)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 178.308 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "779ef623-df89-4ece-ae45-3ae65bb63591")
	)
	(text "Click wheel electrodes: 0.5 mm FPC (J501) or 2.54 mm header (J502), wired in parallel:\n1 top, 2 right, 3 bottom, 4 left, 5 GND, 6 center (pins 1-5 as the clickwheel symbol).\nUse one at a time: the unused one only adds a little stray capacitance.\nJ501: Jushuo AFC07-S06FCA-00 (LCSC C262553), bottom contact, slide lock."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.194 48.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8c9d1053-da45-4a2e-85a1-19510cbf143f")
	)
	(text "MPR121 on the always-on +3.3V (it shares I2C1, see the back-powering rules).\nJP501: cut to measure its drain."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.956 95.504 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9bdbd097-15e6-41db-8c49-d2202671dd17")
	)
	(text "ON/OFF Hold"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 142.24 71.882 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "be071ebb-8f4a-4e15-863f-acf4f96700b5")
	)
	(text "Click-wheel buttons, soldered on this board under the wheel. Active low, 10k pull-ups (as the\nclick-wheel devboard). BTN_* on PE11-PE15 (EXTI11-15)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.706 145.542 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cbb392df-bd74-4c79-b14e-976823734af5")
	)
